# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — TRAILING-COMMA axis.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_comma_axis`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# The ratified asymmetry, in one file (Core #12 — this file samples the `comma`
# axis ONLY):
#   cm_fill     fill-broken       NO trailing comma: the close follows the last
#                                 element inline, so there is nothing for a
#                                 trailing comma to sit before.
#   cm_over     over-width single NO trailing comma either — the lone element is
#                                 also the last one.
#   cm_comment  comment-broken    KEEPS the trailing comma, one element per line.
#                                 A list with an INTERIOR COMMENT cannot be
#                                 packed (the packer's elements are pre-rendered
#                                 strings from a sub-formatter with an empty
#                                 comment sideband), so the delimited-list
#                                 chokepoint diverts it to
#                                 `format_bracketed_broken_with_comments`, whose
#                                 shape is unchanged by this track.
#
# RED source per row: cm_fill / cm_over are TRUE pre-fix REDs (pre-fix they DO
# carry a trailing comma). cm_comment is INVARIANT by design — it is the control
# that proves the two shapes stayed distinct; its red is break-and-restore
# (make `emit_delimited_list` ignore its `Gate` and always pre-render, and the
# comment is re-parented out of the literal entirely).
void cm_fill():
    Vector[int] a = [111111, 222222, 333333, 444444, 555555, 666666, 777777, 888888, 999999, 101010, 111011, 121212, 131313]

void cm_over():
    Vector[int] b = [aSingleArrayElementIdentifierWhoseRenderedWidthAloneExceedsTheEntireLineWidthBudgetOfTheGorgetFormatter]

void cm_comment():
    Vector[int] c = [
        111111,  # first
        222222,
        333333,
    ]
